# What the image build does NOT need. Everything here is large, machine-local,
# rebuilt inside the image anyway, or secret.

# Machine-local secrets. `.mise.local.toml` carries provider API keys on a dev
# box; nothing in an image may ever see them.
.mise.local.toml
.env
.env.*

# Rebuilt in the web stage from the lockfile; also the single largest directory
# in the tree.
**/node_modules

# Build output and the dev substrate's state.
bin/
.dev/
*.log

# History and CI definitions. Dropping .git also settles VCS stamping: the
# runtime image reports the fallback build rather than depending on a git
# binary the golang:alpine stage does not carry. Release binaries are stamped
# by goreleaser OUTSIDE docker, where the repository is whole.
.git
.github

# A console somebody built in this tree. The web stage rebuilds dist from the
# lockfile, so a stale one here is bytes in the context and nothing else. The
# release build reads the console from a context goreleaser lays out, which
# this file never applies to.
web/console/dist
